## Setting

Use the G3CD terminal good-fiber operator at `(11, gamma - 3)` and split its
B103 Hodge ordering after the first 248 H20 coordinates:

```text
K_C = [[A, U],
       [L, J]],

H20 dimension       = 248,
H11 + H02 dimension = 1261.
```

The selected G3CC source has no H20 component, so write it as

```text
b_C = (0, b_lower).
```

This is an exact block decomposition of the emitted G3CD matrix. It does not
truncate a residue sector or alter the selected source.

## Theorem

The lower H11+H02 block satisfies

```text
det(J) = 4 mod 11.
```

Hence `J` is invertible over `GF(11)`. Define the exact response and source
solutions

```text
X = J^-1 L,
y = J^-1 b_lower,
```

and the H20 Schur data

```text
S_C   = A - U X,
b_eff = -U y.
```

The emitted objects have

```text
S_C in Mat_248(GF(11)),   nnz(S_C)   = 55,881,
b_eff in GF(11)^248,      nnz(b_eff) = 226.
```

Their exact ranks and obstruction are

```text
rank(S_C) = 247,
ell_S^T b_eff = 2 mod 11,
rank([[S_C, b_eff], [0, 0]]) = 248.
```

The rank-247 statement is certified above by a normalized nonzero right-null
vector and below by a 247-square minor with determinant `6 mod 11`. The left
null vector is normalized independently. Adjoining `b_eff` gives a nonzero
248-square minor, so the reduced affine rank is exactly 248.

Finally, the reduced witnesses reconstruct the full G3CD witnesses:

```text
r_C   = (r_S,   -J^-1 L r_S),
ell_C = (ell_S, -J^-T U^T ell_S),

ell_C^T b_C = ell_S^T b_eff = 2 mod 11.
```

Thus the static rank/cokernel problem for the 249-dimensional affine Schur
matrix is exactly equivalent to that for the complete 1,510-dimensional G3CD
affine matrix at this fiber. No kernel, cokernel, or selected-source
obstruction is lost.

## Proof

Apply the invertible block row operation

```text
R_top <- R_top - U J^-1 R_lower
```

to the augmented G3CD matrix

```text
[[A, U, 0      ],
 [L, J, b_lower]].
```

It gives

```text
[[S_C, 0, b_eff ],
 [L,   J, b_lower]].
```

Because `J` is invertible, the lower 1,261 coordinates can be solved uniquely
and eliminated. The remaining affine rank contribution is therefore exactly
the rank of `[S_C | b_eff]`. The emitted null formulas are the corresponding
back-substitution identities.

The independent verifier recomputes `det(J)` from the original G3CD dense
matrix, checks all 249 stored lower solves by direct multiplication, rebuilds
`S_C` and `b_eff`, recomputes the rank minors, and verifies both full null
reconstructions and the common pairing.

## Interpretation and boundary

G3CE removes a computational obstacle for static obstruction tests rather than
a physical hypothesis. It does **not** by itself reduce the selected
rank-1,510 transport equation. Block row elimination preserves matrix rank and
cokernel, but a connection ODE is preserved only by a differentiable gauge or
invariant-graph transformation, including the derivative of that
transformation. A separate Riccati identity is required before the lower 1,261
dynamic coordinates can be eliminated.

The unit reduction of `det(J)` also proves that the corresponding canonical
lower block has nonzero characteristic-zero determinant wherever this chart
model is defined. It does not reconstruct the characteristic-zero entries of
`J^-1`, prove that the rank-247 Schur defect persists in characteristic zero,
or establish invertibility at every point of the G3BJ path.

G3CE therefore does not integrate the selected path, reduce its transport
dimension, provide an integral B89 marking, or decide `beta_C`. The next
object is the dynamic invariant-graph/Riccati test. If it fails, the full
rank-1,510 affine continuation remains necessary, with G3CE serving as a
static obstruction certificate and possible preconditioner.

